    "b-ks2-path-run-intro": {
      "id": "b-ks2-path-run-intro",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "RUN CLOSED — The attempt pathway ("
        },
        {
          "insert": "index_task.pathway",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " "
        },
        {
          "insert": "run_closed",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": "). Fires when a worker run closes. The worker summary agent runs once, from a single prompt, and writes the run object — the "
        },
        {
          "insert": "worker_run",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " row and its "
        },
        {
          "insert": "submission",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " rows: hypothesis, scored tries, outcomes — then enqueues an attempt index task. It summarizes and proposes; it never writes a fact — the librarian decides whether anything the run learned changes what is on the page."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-ks2-path-run-agents-heading": {
      "id": "b-ks2-path-run-agents-heading",
      "type": "heading",
      "props": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Agents called"
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-ks2-path-run-agents-table": {
      "id": "b-ks2-path-run-agents-table",
      "type": "structured-table",
      "props": {
        "columns": [
          "Order",
          "Agent",
          "Does"
        ],
        "rows": [
          [
            "1",
            "Worker summary agent",
            [
              {
                "insert": "At run close, from a single prompt: writes the "
              },
              {
                "insert": "worker_run",
                "attributes": {
                  "code": true
                }
              },
              {
                "insert": " row and its "
              },
              {
                "insert": "submission",
                "attributes": {
                  "code": true
                }
              },
              {
                "insert": " rows plus a fact proposal, advances the "
              },
              {
                "insert": "attempt",
                "attributes": {
                  "code": true
                }
              },
              {
                "insert": " watermark, enqueues the index task. Never writes facts"
              }
            ]
          ],
          [
            "2",
            "Librarian",
            [
              {
                "insert": "Consumes the task: reads the run object and the proposal, decides per touched target or entity whether the facts change, searches the sources for corroboration, overwrites live "
              },
              {
                "insert": "fact",
                "attributes": {
                  "code": true
                }
              },
              {
                "insert": " rows with "
              },
              {
                "insert": "attempt://",
                "attributes": {
                  "code": true
                }
              },
              {
                "insert": " citations"
              }
            ]
          ]
        ]
      },
      "children": []
    },
    "b-ks2-path-run-conflict": {
      "id": "b-ks2-path-run-conflict",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "After close, integration either lands — "
        },
        {
          "insert": "worker_run.integration",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " "
        },
        {
          "insert": "integrated",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " — or conflicts: upstream moved, or another worker's merge landed first on the file. No agent resolves the conflict: the run-loop deterministically inserts a "
        },
        {
          "insert": "regression",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " event with "
        },
        {
          "insert": "cause",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " "
        },
        {
          "insert": "merge_conflict",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " and re-queues the target for the next epoch, and the next worker picks up from the ledger. The summary agent runs in both cases — the knowledge is not wasted — and the librarian needs no extra pathway: the event flows through the regression pathway."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-ks2-path-run-librarian-heading": {
      "id": "b-ks2-path-run-librarian-heading",
      "type": "heading",
      "props": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Librarian operation"
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-ks2-path-run-librarian-reads": {
      "id": "b-ks2-path-run-librarian-reads",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "The librarian reads the "
        },
        {
          "insert": "worker_run",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " row, its "
        },
        {
          "insert": "submission",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " rows, and the proposal, alongside the live "
        },
        {
          "insert": "fact",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " rows for "
        },
        {
          "insert": "worker_run.target_id",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ". The run's target is the subject first; a submission that leaned on a struct, a field, or a neighbouring function puts that entity's facts in scope too. Search runs against the source surfaces — the librarian is the only agent that does: the structured attempts query (target, outcome, score trajectory) is the first query, keyword over hypotheses and transcripts follows, the code graph checks a claim against the checkout, and archival keyword and vector search corroborate when the run's claims echo something Discord, a PR, or the wiki already said."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-ks2-path-run-librarian-writes": {
      "id": "b-ks2-path-run-librarian-writes",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Every write goes through the resolver. The affected live "
        },
        {
          "insert": "fact",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " rows are overwritten in place, each fact's "
        },
        {
          "insert": "evidence",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " rows replaced wholesale — "
        },
        {
          "insert": "attempt://run/<worker_run.id>[/submission/<seq>]",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " locators into the run and its scored tries, plus whatever corroboration the search returned. A run outcome never becomes a fact by itself, and a tested hypothesis that failed stays on the ledger side, citable later as "
        },
        {
          "insert": "attempt://",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " evidence. A resolution move that keeps recurring across runs may be filed as a "
        },
        {
          "insert": "pattern",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " fact — the "
        },
        {
          "insert": "pattern",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " entity is curated, and the librarian is its only writer."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
